Okay, first things first: FUCK GOOGLE.
I know for a FACT they make it very obscure and hard to make it so
you dont have to drop a <link rel="preconnect" href="https://bullshit.google.com/">
and connect to their services just to get a few fonts on a website.

Like, when you get fonts from <fonts.google.com>, they give you an option:
1. Download the font files as ttf without any choice on what format they are
2. Embed the fonts to a website using google chatgpt ai generated code and by dropping
   several connections to googles servers so they can probably track your users.

It very much feels like google only offers the download option so people won't compain
about the second thing and that if you're gonna use fonts on a website, its GOTTA 
connect to fonts.gshatit.com and whatever other google services. 
They probably think that I'm thinking "well, its a website, its gotta connect to the 
internet anyways" but what I'm more thinking is "I don't want google shoving its large 
size 3ft ad dildo up my websites ass and then tracking my users with it." 

You may ask, "but Dutch, why would they track us?" And I do agree, that sounds 
conspiritorial as hell, but they actually do track you. Hell, they could be using their 
google chrome mind powers to send them data about the last thing you typed in the 
URL/search bar as we speak...

Yes, they say they use this data to improve their services, but this simply isnt that
true.

It has been basically proven that, they legally CAN do this, but they collect your
data, then sell it to advertisers, who will show you ads based on that data, and pay
big pappa G a few cents for every ad you "see"(sometimes on some websites you dont even 
really see some of the ads as theres already 1000 other ads plastered across said site).

Think about it, you ever google something or look for a YouTube video, just to get an ad
related to said search on a completely different website? like, lets say, you look for 
cat videos on YouTube, just to later see an ad for something like cat food or even a pet
store on Instagram or Facebook, thats a result of google tracking you. 

Its not like most people assume when somebody says someones tracking someone, though, 
they just track your internet activity, such as the websites you go to and the data you 
send those sites. 

Its not like they're the FBI on the hunt for jeffery epstein because that would 
mean they don't even try to track you in the first place. Its not like you've been 
evading your taxes for the past decade and are now being followed by the IRS, but it is 
like having a pervert peek through your window when you go to sleep at night; Hes not
exactly doing anything at the moment, but its not like you're fine with bro being there.

Google will do what they can to make that bottom line, as long as it wont ruin their 
public image and keep that illusion that they care about you. Maybe the devs at google
care, but definitely not the execs, chairmen, supervisors and ceos. Hell, the execs at 
google care so much about optimizing that bottom line that they've started replacing
some of their own employees with ai. Hell, thats why most generative ai exists in the 
first place, so you(and google) dont have to pay a real person to make real art, 
or write a real sentence. 

And whilst I'm not completely against the idea of ai as a TOOL to ASSIST with tasks like
raytracing and stuff that would take hours of work for the most minimal effects and 
things like that, I am against the idea of "ai art" in the sense that typing some
words in a computer text box and having the computer make something out of that isn't
art. It didnt come from your heart, you didnt spend hours or even just minutes on that
drawing, its just something a comouter spat out. Computer generated interpolation frames
arent considered art, why is this? 

I don't rember who said this, but I've always agreed with this philosophy and the guy 
who said this figured out how to put it into words:
| Human beings are energy, and one
| of the best things a human can do
| is take that energy and put it
| back into the world, in the form
| of a drawing, a story, whatever,
| as long as that energy is being
| put back into the world, its art.

Ai isnt human energy, its ai. The most human thing about ai art are the prompts used to 
generate it, and those don't have a lot of energy.

It doesnt matter how that energy is put into the world, whether its singing, dancing,
writing, drawing, taking pictures and videos, as long as its from a real human being,
and not drawn, written or sung by chatgpt, its art. 

Notice how ai "artists" always have to argue with others whether their "art" is art or 
not? Doesn't really happen when you put time and effort into something, because people 
generally understand that you put your time and effort into that thing, and won't 
really argue with you if you were to call it "your masterpiece" because they know,
to you, it is...

...Unless they use twitt- erm im sorry i mean X.com where people are too
busy watching those X videos to think about the time and effort put into something
and have arguably been brainwashed by elon's musk and his ai son grok.

